/target

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Editors
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# Local caches and crash reports (ebman writes to ~/.cache; safety net for any in-tree runs)
*.log
crash-*.log

# Claude Code working directory
.claude/

# candor: the scan reports are derived artefacts (regenerate with
# `candor-scan .`) and `deps/` is a per-machine cache — but the
# POLICY is source and must be tracked, or the CI gate has nothing to
# read. This used to ignore `.candor/` wholesale, which would have
# shipped a gate with no policy behind it.
.candor/report.*.json
.candor/deps/
.candor/cache/

# cargo-mutants working directories. Never commit these: a local sweep
# writes `lock.json` containing the machine's hostname and username, and
# the whole tree is regenerated output that rotates to `mutants.out.old/`
# on each run — so committing it grows history permanently AND ships
# personal detail to crates.io. Both happened: v0.34.1 published 22 of
# these files, lock.json included.
mutants.out/
mutants.out.old/

# Editor / tooling backups. `sed -i.bak` writes these IN PLACE, and a
# `git add -A` then sweeps them in — which is how a 55KB copy of a test
# file was committed and would have shipped inside the 0.36.0 crate.
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
